==========================================================================
PART 3 — exact resonant-product cap at n=27 (=3*9), the only nontrivial 2-factor
==========================================================================
  e(K3)=3 (=3=u(3)); densest 9-lattice patch e=16 (=16=Harborth(9) < u(9)=18)
  ChordSpec(K3)={1: 3}  -> chord-free (only norm 1)
  ChordSpec(3x3 patch)={1: 16, 4: 7, 3: 8, 7: 4, 12: 1}

  resonant U over (3-factor) (+)_t (3x3 9-patch), scan t=2..30:
         3-factor  e  best_t  Delta    U
               K3  3    None      0   75
       path(120°)  2       3      4   70
   path(straight)  2       4      3   69
  Analytic bound: U(27,resonant) = 9*e(G3)+3*e(H9)+Delta_t,
    e(H9)<=Harborth(9)=16, Delta_t<=8*(3-e(G3))  =>  U <= e(G3)+72 <= 75.
    (With only the planar bound e(H9)<=u(9)=18: U <= e(G3)+78 <= 81.)
  => no 2-factor RESONANT product beats 81 at 27; exact cap 75 (resonance HURTS).

