    n  P_gen     arg   3n  gap  LP-chord factrzn (parts<=8, >=1 size>=4)
   24     66 (2, 12)   72    6                          [(3, 8), (4, 6)]
   25     70  (5, 5)   75    5                                  [(5, 5)]
   26     73 (2, 13)   78    5                                        []
   27     81  (3, 9)   81    0                                        []
   28     83  (4, 7)   84    1                                  [(4, 7)]
  n=24 (LP 4x6,3x8): gap 6 too big;  n=25 (LP 5x5): gap 5 too big;
  n=26 (only 2x13, 13 imperfect): no LP factorization;
  n=27 (only 3x9, 9 imperfect; 3 chord-free): excluded -- generic merely TIES 81;
  n=28 (LP 4x7): gap=1 < Delta_3=2  =>  FIRST resonant crossing.

==========================================================================
PART 5 — explicit n=28 resonant crossing  W7 (+)_3 R = 85 > 84  (exact)
==========================================================================
  e(W7)=12, e(R)=5, |W7|=7, |R|=4
  generic Cartesian P(28) = 12*4 + 7*5 = 83
  Delta_3(R,W7) = 2
  U(W7 (+)_3 R) = 83 + 2 = 85  vs 3*28 = 84  -> CROSS
  sizes 4,7 lattice-perfect: Harborth(4)=u(4)=5=5, Harborth(7)=u(7)=12=12
  ChordSpec(R)={1: 5, 3: 1}  -> non-unit chord norm 3 (sqrt3) present

